From: iyanz <boooky10@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AntiXray particle line-of-sight gate

Adds an opt-in per-(player, particle-origin) line-of-sight check
inside ServerLevel.sendParticles (private per-player overload) so that
when antixray.particle-raytrace.enabled = true, particles emitted
behind solid blocks from the receiver's POV are dropped before
player.connection.send(packet).

Closes the wallhack signal that ore-pillar / door-frame particles
would otherwise leak. Toggle off by default; off-by-default also
preserves vanilla "you can hear/see fire spread behind a wall" feel.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
index 1e19dc5395cf0a14c1a9aeab83ac39d2e66d181a..a78949384771efdffc11380d4dcfdb405018bfdb 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -2201,6 +2201,12 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements WorldGenLevel, ServerEntityGet
         } else {
             BlockPos pos = player.blockPosition();
             if (pos.closerToCenterThan(new Vec3(x, y, z), overrideLimiter ? 512.0 : 32.0)) {
+                // SourbyCraft start - particle ray-trace gate
+                if (dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.antixray.ParticleVisibilityCheck.ENABLED.get()
+                    && !dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.antixray.ParticleVisibilityCheck.canSee(player, x, y, z)) {
+                    return false;
+                }
+                // SourbyCraft end - particle ray-trace gate
                 player.connection.send(packet);
                 return true;
             } else {
